# Allowlist, not a denylist.
#
# This repo is public and mirrors a directory that other programs write into.
# A denylist would mean predicting every filename a future Claude Code release
# invents — session transcripts, oauth artifacts, plugin caches, lock files.
# Deny everything, then re-admit exactly what belongs here. Unknown files fail
# closed.

*

!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!LICENSE
!install.sh
!bootstrap-linux.sh

!.githooks/
!.githooks/**

!lib/
!lib/**

!settings/
!settings/*.json

!claude/
!claude/CLAUDE.md
!claude/projects-CLAUDE.md
!claude/statusline-command.sh
!claude/hooks/
!claude/hooks/*.sh
!claude/bin/
!claude/bin/*.sh

!skills/
!skills/**

!mcp/
!mcp/*.json

!dcg/
!dcg/config.toml

# Only the templates. The real local layer lives at ~/.claude/local/, outside
# this tree, precisely so it cannot be committed by accident.
!local/
!local/README.md
!local/*.example

# Personal list of words that must never appear in tracked files. It is a list
# of the things being kept private, so it stays private itself.
.scrub-words

# Never, under any pattern.
**/.env
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/.credentials.json
**/settings.local.json
**/local.env
